# beatmania IIDX (GQ863 VER. JAA), Konami 1999: as bmiidx-play.his.
# beatmania IIDX (1st style, Twinkle): a scripted game from the NVRAM bmiidx-clear leaves
# (backup RAM cleared). Three coins (a credit at the default price), 1P Start on the title,
# 7KEYS at mode select, a key at sound select, then the first stage played with a fixed
# pattern: the seven keys in turn and turntable spins in both directions, to the result.
# Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, against MAME with the DVD
# player's CTS (PLAN.md section 21, TW-5).
game bmiidxa

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 1800 press "Coin 1" 8
at 1830 press "Coin 1" 8
at 1860 press "Coin 1" 8
at 2700 press "1 Player Start" 8
# mode select, its cursor on 4KEYS: one turntable spin moves it (round) to 7KEYS, SW1 takes it
at 2950 set "1P Table" 6
at 2951 set "1P Table" 12
at 2952 set "1P Table" 18
at 2953 set "1P Table" 24
at 2954 set "1P Table" 30
at 2955 set "1P Table" 36
at 2956 set "1P Table" 42
at 2957 set "1P Table" 48
at 2958 set "1P Table" 54
at 2959 set "1P Table" 60
at 2960 set "1P Table" 66
at 2961 set "1P Table" 72
at 2962 set "1P Table" 78
at 2963 set "1P Table" 84
at 2964 set "1P Table" 90
at 2965 set "1P Table" 96
at 3150 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3600 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8       # sound select: the song under the cursor
# the stage: a key every 9 frames, 1 to 7 in turn; a turntable spin every 120 frames, 16 frames
# of 6 steps a frame, alternating direction
at 4400 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 4
at 4409 press "P1-2 (SW2)" 4
at 4418 press "P1-3 (SW3)" 4
at 4427 press "P1-4 (SW4)" 4
at 4436 press "P1-5 (SW5)" 4
